# Appointment Update & Cancellation Walkthrough

I have successfully implemented the architecture plan to safely allow the agent to update and cancel existing appointments!

## 1. The `cancel_consultation` Tool
I created a new dedicated tool: [cancel_consultation.py](file:///d:/Final_calling_agent/agent/tools/cancel_consultation.py).
This tool cleanly separates the cancellation logic from the booking logic. It uses the existing API endpoint but modifies the payload:
- Sends `"status": "cancelled"` to the backend.
- Prefixes the provided `reason` into the message field (e.g., `CANCELLATION REASON: User no longer needs it.`), ensuring your clinical coordinators know *why* the cancellation occurred.

## 2. Programmatic Guardrail
To guarantee that the LLM cannot skip your "Ask Why First" rule, I implemented a stateful guardrail in the [VoicePipelineOrchestrator](file:///d:/Final_calling_agent/agent/pipeline.py#L161-L503).
- The pipeline now tracks `self._cancellation_save_attempted`.
- If the AI tries to cancel the appointment on the first request, the tool immediately blocks the API call and forces the AI to reply: *"SYSTEM GUARDRAIL: Do not cancel yet. First politely ask the caller why they want to cancel and if you can help resolve their issue."*
- Once the AI asks why, the tool unlocks, allowing the cancellation to proceed on the next turn if the user insists.

## 3. Conversational Guardrails
I updated the core instructions in [guardrails.md](file:///d:/Final_calling_agent/agent/prompts/core/guardrails.md#L57-L63) with a strict `CANCELLATION POLICY`.
This instructs Kiara to:
- **Rule A:** Never proactively offer cancellation.
- **Rule B:** Always make a save attempt first.
- **Rule C:** Execute the cancellation if the user insists.
- **Rule D:** Confirm the cancellation verbally *only after* the backend returns success.

## 4. Updates (Already Working)
As discussed, updating an appointment already works perfectly through the existing `book_consultation` tool! Whenever the user changes their city or dentist, the tool simply passes the existing `lead_id`, which performs an "upsert" on the CRM backend. I added instructions to ensure Kiara explicitly asks for confirmation before updating any details.

> [!TIP]
> **Testing it out:** Try starting a call, booking an appointment, and then say *"I want to cancel"*. Kiara will now attempt to save the appointment first. If you insist, she will seamlessly cancel it!
